  "question": {
    "text": "Three concentric metallic spherical shells of radii $R, 2 R, 3 R$ are given charges $Q_1, Q_2, Q_3$, respectively. It is found that the surface charge densities on the outer surfaces of the shells are equal. Then, the ratio of the charges given to the shells, $Q_1: Q_2: Q_3$, is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ysMBh",
      "text": "\n$1: 2: 3$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "V4qjI",
      "text": "\n$1: 3: 5$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ohE0w",
      "text": "\n$1: 4: 9$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "zFIZU",
      "text": "\n$1: 8: 18$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$Q_1=\\sigma\\left(4 \\pi R^2\\right)=4 \\pi \\sigma R^2$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& Q_2=16 \\pi \\sigma R^2-Q_1=12 \\pi \\sigma R^2 \\\\\n& Q_3=36 \\pi \\sigma R^2-16 \\pi \\sigma R^2=20 \\pi \\sigma R^2 \\\\\n& Q_1: Q_2: Q_3=1: 3: 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/Jz5mCEist3pR1NMXu_D_hDCaSA1XV59ytfACfkSpAiA.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
